## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: If a user is granted "Full Control" via Share Permissions, but only "Read" via NTFS permissions, what can they do to the files over the network?
A1: They can only Read. When Share and NTFS permissions conflict, the most restrictive permission always applies.

Q2: Why do we disable inheritance when creating a new department share?
A2: By default, the `C:\` drive grants the local `Users` group Read access. If inheritance is not disabled, every employee in the company will automatically inherit read access to sensitive department files.